    expectedAnswer: "Sliding-window maximum is solved efficiently with a monotonic deque of indices. The deque stores candidates in decreasing value order and removes indexes that leave the window from the front.",
    deepExplanation: "Step 1 — Keep deque values decreasing.\n\nWITHOUT BUILT-IN / CORE:\n```ts\nfunction maxSlidingWindow(\n  nums: readonly number[],\n  k: number,\n): number[] {\n  if (k <= 0 || nums.length === 0 || k > nums.length) {\n    return [];\n  }\n\n  const deque: number[] = [];\n  let front = 0;\n  const result: number[] = [];\n\n  for (let i = 0; i < nums.length; i++) {\n    // Remove indexes outside the window.\n    if (\n      front < deque.length &&\n      deque[front]! <= i - k\n    ) {\n      front++;\n    }\n\n    // Remove smaller values from the back.\n    while (\n      deque.length > front &&\n      nums[deque[deque.length - 1]!]! <= nums[i]!\n    ) {\n      deque.pop();\n    }\n\n    deque.push(i);\n\n    if (i >= k - 1) {\n      result.push(nums[deque[front]!]!);\n    }\n  }\n\n  return result;\n}\n```\n\nWITH BUILT-IN:\n```ts\nfunction maxSlidingWindowUsingBuiltIns(\n  nums: readonly number[],\n  k: number,\n): number[] {\n  const result: number[] = [];\n\n  for (let start = 0; start + k <= nums.length; start++) {\n    let best = nums[start]!;\n\n    for (let i = start + 1; i < start + k; i++) {\n      best = Math.max(best, nums[i]!);\n    }\n\n    result.push(best);\n  }\n\n  return result;\n}\n```\n\nStep 2 — Example:\nnums=[1,3,-1,-3,5,3,6,7], k=3\nwindows:\n[1,3,-1] → 3\n[3,-1,-3] → 3\n[-1,-3,5] → 5\n...\nanswer [3,3,5,5,6,7].\n\nStep 3 — Complexity:\nMonotonic deque O(n) time and O(k) auxiliary space.\nNaive built-in-friendly scan O(nk).",
