    deepExplanation: "Step 1 — Simple sliding-window counter.\n\nWITHOUT BUILT-IN / CORE:\n```ts\nclass SlidingWindowLimiter {\n  private readonly timestamps: number[] = [];\n  private front = 0;\n\n  constructor(\n    private readonly maxRequests: number,\n    private readonly windowMs: number,\n  ) {}\n\n  allow(now: number): boolean {\n    while (\n      this.front < this.timestamps.length &&\n      this.timestamps[this.front]! <= now - this.windowMs\n    ) {\n      this.front++;\n    }\n\n    if (this.timestamps.length - this.front >= this.maxRequests) {\n      return false;\n    }\n\n    this.timestamps.push(now);\n    return true;\n  }\n}\n```\n\nWITH BUILT-IN-friendly:\n```ts\nfunction createTokenBucket(\n  capacity: number,\n  refillPerSecond: number,\n) {\n  let tokens = capacity;\n  let last = Date.now();\n\n  return {\n    tryConsume(now = Date.now()): boolean {\n      const elapsedSeconds = (now - last) / 1000;\n\n      tokens = Math.min(\n        capacity,\n        tokens + elapsedSeconds * refillPerSecond,\n      );\n      last = now;\n\n      if (tokens < 1) return false;\n\n      tokens -= 1;\n      return true;\n    },\n  };\n}\n```\n\nStep 2 — Example:\nlimit = 3 requests / 1000ms\ntimestamps [100,200,300]\nat time 400 → reject\nat time 1200 → old timestamps expire and a new request may pass.\n\nStep 3 — Complexity:\nAmortized O(1) per request with a moving front.\nSpace O(number of requests in the window).\n\nStep 4 — Production rule:\nFor distributed systems, enforce limits centrally or consistently across instances.",
